{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-categorical-lagrangian-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:categorical-lagrangian-intro","kind":"prose","text":"categorical-lagrangian-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:categorical-lagrangian-intro\"></a><p>The categorical Dirac operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla</code> combines with a state <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code> to form the endomorphism of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> that will be traced to yield the action. The categorical Lagrangian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_q(\\nabla, \\psi) = \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla^2 + \\psi^* \\otimes \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla\\psi \\in \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code> packages the bosonic and fermionic sectors before trace-integration. This endomorphism exists uniquely once <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> are chosen.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-categorical-lagrangian-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":56,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
